{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And a river</b> — before man was created, the river was watering the garden on every side." "The alef of the word ראשים is a root letter, as is seen in the word מַרְאֲשוֹתֵיכֶם (\"at your heads\"), and its meaning is [related to] honoring the head."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "Reading וטעמו מכבד הראש ('its meaning is honoring the head'); one manuscript tradition reads מכבר הראש, marked here by the abbreviation נ\"א (= נוסח אחר, 'variant reading'), the sense of which is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:48.260053124Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}